583 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 189 0 R/T(6. Coalition-Building and Regional Cooperation)/E(6. Coalition-Building and Regional Cooperation)/Pg 23 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

584 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 189 0 R/E(No military campaign in Afghanistan was possible without regional cooperation, and the most essential partner was Pakistan \204 a state that had until that week been one of the Taliban's principal international backers.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

585 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 189 0 R/E(The demands placed on Islamabad were substantial, and the domestic risks of compliance were severe. What can reasonably be asked of a partner state whose own stability may be threatened by cooperation? What should be offered in return? And what happens to the relationship when the immediate crisis passes?)/Pg 23 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

586 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 189 0 R/T(7. Preventing the Next Attack)/E(7. Preventing the Next Attack)/Pg 23 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

587 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 189 0 R/E(Retaliation addresses what has already happened. Prevention addresses what has not yet happened, and it is the harder problem.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

588 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 189 0 R/E(Intelligence reform, aviation security, border controls, financial tracking, and international information-sharing all featured in the response. Each carries costs \204 financial, diplomatic, and in terms of individual liberty. Which measures actually reduce risk, and which merely provide the appearance of action?)/Pg 23 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

