1035 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(The following questions define what this committee is expected to resolve. Any directive, resolution, or set of measures produced by this body should engage substantively with them. Delegates should prepare positions on each before committee begins.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1036 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(1. What standard of evidence must be satisfied before responsibility for the attacks is formally attributed, and to whom must that evidence be disclosed \204 the Security Council, allied governments, or the public?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1037 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(2. Should the attacks be treated as an act of war or as a criminal act, and what legal framework consequently governs the response \204 the law of armed conflict, or domestic and international criminal law?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1038 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(3. Under what circumstances does providing sanctuary to a non-state armed group render a state legally responsible for that group's actions, and what measures may lawfully be taken against such a state?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1039 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(4. How should the right of self-defence under Article 51 of the UN Charter be interpreted and bounded when the attacking party is a non-state actor, and what limits apply to its duration, geographic scope, and objectives?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1040 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(5. What expansion of surveillance, detention, and investigative powers is justified in response to this threat, what oversight must accompany it, and what mechanisms should govern its eventual withdrawal?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

1041 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(6. What can reasonably be required of regional partner states whose cooperation is essential to any response, what should be offered in return, and how should the domestic risks borne by those partners be accounted for?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

1042 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 204 0 R/E(7. What structural reforms to intelligence coordination, aviation security, border control, and terrorist financing should be adopted to reduce the likelihood of a comparable attack, and how should their effectiveness be measured?)/Pg 38 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

